00:07:02.820 --> 00:07:04.880
So let's start with explaining that

00:07:04.880 --> 00:07:09.060
the average human bladder
holds 16 ounces of urine,

00:07:09.060 --> 00:07:13.310
which is two cupful, two
cupfuls of urine literally.

00:07:13.310 --> 00:07:14.640
So these are eight ounces each.

00:07:14.640 --> 00:07:16.380
Letting your brain know
when it's time to go

00:07:16.380 --> 00:07:17.930
is a really complex process.

00:07:17.930 --> 00:07:19.900
So if you continuously
strain your bladder,

00:07:19.900 --> 00:07:22.180
you could actually cause
yourself some serious problems.

00:07:22.180 --> 00:07:24.350
You may retain urine after you urinate,

00:07:24.350 --> 00:07:26.560
you don't have control
over your urination,

00:07:26.560 --> 00:07:28.730
you could potentially have an increase

00:07:28.730 --> 00:07:30.210
in urinary tract infections.

00:07:30.210 --> 00:07:31.540
This isn't necessarily proven.

00:07:31.540 --> 00:07:32.720
Logically make sense

00:07:32.720 --> 00:07:35.000
that if you're keeping
that urine stagnant,

00:07:35.000 --> 00:07:37.960
that bacteria has a higher
chance to multiply in that area.

00:07:37.960 --> 00:07:40.670
But look, if you're just
holding it for a few minutes,

00:07:40.670 --> 00:07:42.800
hour or two, it's not a big deal.

00:07:42.800 --> 00:07:45.130
Know that your initial urge to go urinate

00:07:45.130 --> 00:07:47.370
usually happens when your
bladder is about half full.

00:07:47.370 --> 00:07:49.090
That's a good time for
you to go and urinate.

00:07:49.090 --> 00:07:50.910
But if you need to wait an hour or two,

00:07:50.910 --> 00:07:51.820
your body can handle it.

